#TIME AND SPACE COMPLEXITY ANALYSIS

Snippet 1: find_max
Time: O(n) | Space: O(1)
Justification: Single linear scan, only one variable stored.

Snippet 2: has_duplicate
Time: O(n^2) | Space: O(1)
Justification: Nested loops compare every pair, no extra DS.

Snippet 3: sum_digits
Time: O(d) = O(log n) | Space: O(d)
Justification: One recursive call per digit, recursion stack = d.

Snippet 4: print_pairs
Time: O(n^2) | Space: O(n^2)
Justification: n*n iterations storing n^2 pairs.

Snippet 5: binary_search
Time: O(log n) | Space: O(1)
Justification: Halves search space each time, only pointers used.

Snippet 6: matrix_multiply
Time: O(n^3) | Space: O(n^2)
Justification: Three nested loops for n x n, result is n^2.

Snippet 7: to_sparse
Time: O(m*n) | Space: O(k)
Justification: Visits all m*n cells, stores only k non-zero elements.

Snippet 8: process
Time: O(n + n^2) = O(n^2)
Justification: First loop O(n) + nested loop O(n^2).

Snippet 9: check_first_ten
Time: O(n)
Justification: Inner loop constant 10, so 10*n = O(n).

Snippet 10: reverse_new
Time: O(n) | Space: O(n)
Justification: One pass copies n elements to new array.

Snippet 11: reverse_in_place
Time: O(n) | Space: O(1)
Justification: Swaps n/2 times in-place, no extra array.

Snippet 12: factorial
Time: O(n) | Space: O(n)
Justification: n recursive calls, stack depth n.

Snippet 13: fibonacci
Time: O(2^n) | Space: O(n)
Justification: Exponential recursive tree, stack depth n.

Snippet 14: count_pairs_with_sum
Time: O(n) | Space: O(n)
Justification: Single pass with hash set O(1) lookup.

Snippet 15: print_all_subsets
Time: O(n * 2^n)
Justification: 2^n subsets, each checks n bits.

Snippet 16: merge_sorted
Time: O(n+m) | Space: O(n+m)
Justification: Each element visited once, stored in new list.

Snippet 17: is_palindrome
Time: O(n) | Space: O(n)
Justification: s[::-1] creates reversed copy of size n.

Snippet 18: flatten
Time: O(m*n) | Space: O(m*n)
Justification: Visits all m*n elements, stores them.

Snippet 19: power
Time: O(exp) | Space: O(exp)
Justification: One recursive call per decrement.

Snippet 20: fast_power
Time: O(log exp) | Space: O(log exp)
Justification: Halves exponent each call.

Snippet 21: has_common_element
Time: O(n*m) | Space: O(1)
Justification: Compares every element of a with b in worst case.

Snippet 22: build_frequency_map
Time: O(n) | Space: O(n)
Justification: Single pass, map stores up to n unique keys
